id: pm-rl-e20d
title: "pm-rl: an RL programme as tracked project data"
description: "An RL programme is one of the most context-heavy things an agent can run, and today its context lives in a dashboard, a folder of JSON and shell history: not reviewable, not merge-safe, and not available to the agent deciding what to train next. pm-rl makes the programme itself a tracker. Two pm properties do the real work. Metric logging is append-only and so is pm history, which unions losslessly under concurrent writers on separate branches, so two agents sweeping on two branches never lose rows. And runs form a dependency graph pm already models and queries, so the question that actually costs teams weeks - which results does this reward-spec change invalidate - is a reachability query rather than a feature."
type: Epic
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:38:28.906Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-12T23:18:52.981Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-12T23:18:52.963Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-12T23:18:52.963Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 4800
acceptance_criteria: "Every item type registers with typed fields under the host schema; a run's metric series is only ever written to history; two concurrent runs on two branches merge to the union of both series against real git branches; leaderboard and invalidate answer from the dependency graph; 100 percent line, branch, function and docstring coverage"
unblock_note: "Unblocked: pm-cli#854 closed 2026-08-01. The SDK now ships defineBeforeMutationHook and BeforeMutationHook types, verified in node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/dist/sdk/authoring.d.ts. The child pm-rl-et5b is implemented and tested with a real beforeMutation hook."
resolution: All five acceptance criteria satisfied; the host-level write interception blocker is resolved via defineBeforeMutationHook.
expected_result: Every item type registers; metric series in history; two-branch merge unions; leaderboard and invalidate from graph; 100 percent coverage and docstrings.
actual_result: "defineExtension registers all types; series.ts writes to history; test/index.test.ts:569 proves two-branch union; leaderboard.ts and invalidate.ts query the graph; coverage 100/100/100/100, 139 declarations documented, 323 tests pass."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T13:30:17.054Z",pi-agent,"Re-verified this session (pi-agent). Every acceptance criterion in THIS epic is satisfied against the current tree: all nine item types register with typed fields under the host schema; a run's metric series is only ever written to history (never a body); two concurrent writers on two real git branches merge to the union of both series — proven for plain runs and again for independent sweep arms; leaderboard and invalidate answer from the stored dependency graph; npm run coverage reports 17 source file(s) at 100/100/100 lines/branches/functions and npm run docstring reports 17 file(s), 123 declaration(s) documented, with release:check fully green.\n\nThe epic stays BLOCKED for exactly one reason, inherited from its child pm-rl-et5b: host-level write-time interception of arbitrary core mutations (see that item's re-verification note — pm-cli#854 closed without delivering an extension-registerable mutation-invariant hook in 2026.8.20). Nothing else is missing; if et5b unblocks or the fleet agrees use-time detection satisfies its intent, this epic can close immediately on the evidence above.\n"
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T12:08:34.914Z",codex,"First production tranche completed: content-addressed Environment registration/show/list plus attributable Run start/log/show/finish, real installed-host acceptance, exact 100/100/100 coverage, 100% docstring coverage, and real Git two-agent union proof. pm-rl-dyho, pm-rl-fpon, and pm-rl-mpd9 are closed with evidence. pm-rl-et5b remains active only for host-level write interception (pm-cli#854); current commands already detect tampering before use and preserve exact snapshots."
